Yean Chan (ychan@ix.netcom.com) wrote:
: Hi Everybody,
: 	I recently got a driver fix for a CD-ROM game. The game does not 
: copy the driver to the hard disk during installation. How can I update 
: the driver if the game does not have a driver initialization file in the 
: hard disk.
: 	Thanks.

Usually (though there are no guarantees) programs will search the hard 
drive directory specified during setup first, and load any files they 
need from there if found.  This allows programmers like me (well, not too 
much like me-- they have to have made a mistake :) ) to "upgrade" 
programs and data on the fly.  Of course, there is always the possibility 
of calling customer support....

